OL,4,Q]W  5j 5    W\Q] Ffrom JOHANNESBURG
OL,6, The English XI were 149-1 in their
OL,7, second innings after being forced to
OL,8, follow on against South Africa.
OL,10,BOpeners Graham Gooch and Geoff Boycott
OL,11,Bmade a solid start, with Gooch 94 not
OL,12,Bout. Boycott was out lbw to Van der
OL,13,BBijl for 36.
OL,15,BThe English were 150 all out in their
OL,16,Bfirst innings replying to South
OL,17,BAfrica's 400-7 declared on the third
OL,18,Bday of a four-day match.
OL,20,BThey had offered little resistance to
OL,21,Bthe strong seam attack.
OL,23,Q]GFromB14-03-82G/ teletextarchive.com
